@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Green Squirrel Dev</PageTitle>

<div class="container legal-container">
    <header class="legal-header">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Effective date: @EffectiveDate</p>
    </header>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <p>
            Green Squirrel Dev ("Green Squirrel Dev," "we," "us," or "our") is a small, independent software
            studio run by a single developer. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect when you
            use greensquirrel.dev, the Scurry service and browser extension, and any other app or service we operate
            that links to this policy (together, the "Services"), how we use it, and the choices you have.
        </p>
        <p>
            The short version: we collect only what we need to run the Services, we don't sell your data, and
            you can ask us to delete it at any time.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Information you give us</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Account information.</strong> When you sign in with Google, we receive your name, email
                address, profile picture URL, and a unique Google account identifier. We never see or store your
                Google password.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Profile and settings.</strong> Your display name, your Send-to-Kindle email address (if you
                provide one), and your preferences, such as notification and formatting options.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Communications.</strong> If you email us, we keep your message and email address so we can
                reply.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Content you send through the Services</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Articles sent to Kindle.</strong> When you use Scurry, the extension sends the content,
                title, URL, and author of the page you choose to our servers. We convert it into an e-book file and
                email it to the Kindle address you provided. We process this content only to deliver it to you and
                do not keep the article content after it has been sent. Article titles may appear briefly in our
                operational logs.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Usage and device data.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting and monitoring tools record
                technical information such as IP address, browser type, pages visited, timestamps, and error
                details.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use our website
                (for example, which pages are popular). Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Authentication cookies and tokens.</strong> We use cookies and tokens to keep you signed
                in. The browser extension stores a sign-in token in your browser's extension storage.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Provide, operate, and maintain the Services, including signing you in and delivering articles to your Kindle;</li>
            <li>Save your settings and preferences;</li>
            <li>Respond to your questions and support requests;</li>
            <li>Send important service-related messages (we do not send marketing email without your consent);</li>
            <li>Monitor performance, fix bugs, and improve the Services;</li>
            <li>Detect, prevent, and respond to abuse, fraud, or security issues; and</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Where laws such as the GDPR apply, we rely on these legal bases: performing our contract with you
            (providing the Services), our legitimate interests (keeping the Services secure and improving them),
            your consent (for example, analytics cookies where consent is required), and compliance with the law.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. How We Share Your Information</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>We do not sell or rent your personal information</strong>, and we do not share it for
            cross-context behavioral advertising. We share information only in these limited cases:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Service providers.</strong> We use trusted third parties to run the Services, including
                Microsoft Azure (hosting, database, logging, and email delivery), Google (sign-in and analytics), and
                Amazon (when you send content to your Kindle address, it is delivered to Amazon's Send-to-Kindle
                service). These providers process data on our behalf under their own privacy and security terms.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Legal reasons.</strong> If required by law, subpoena, or other legal process, or if we
                believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to protect our rights, your safety, or the safety
                of others.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Business transfers.</strong> If Green Squirrel Dev or one of its products is sold or
                transferred, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction. We will let you know
                before your information becomes subject to a different privacy policy.
            </li>
            <li><strong>With your consent.</strong> In any other case, only when you ask us to.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Browser Extension</h2>
        <p>
            The Scurry browser extension only reads a web page when you click to send it, using the
            <code>activeTab</code> and <code>scripting</code> permissions, and uses <code>storage</code> to keep you signed in.
            It does not track your browsing history or read pages in the background. Data collected through
            the extension is used only to provide its single purpose, sending articles to your Kindle, and is
            not used or transferred for any unrelated purpose, including advertising or creditworthiness. Our use
            of data received from Google APIs follows the Google API Services User Data Policy, including its
            Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
            We keep your account information for as long as your account is active. Article content is processed
            in memory and discarded once it is delivered. Operational logs are kept for a limited period (typically
            up to 90 days) and then deleted. If you delete your account, we delete your personal information within
            30 days, except where we must keep it to comply with law, resolve disputes, or enforce our agreements.
            Backups may persist for a short additional period before being overwritten.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
            We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards to protect your information, including
            encryption in transit (HTTPS), encryption at rest provided by our cloud host, hashed extension tokens,
            and restricted access to production systems. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure,
            so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Access the personal information we hold about you and get a copy of it;</li>
            <li>Correct inaccurate information (you can update your display name and Kindle email in your account settings);</li>
            <li>Delete your account and personal information;</li>
            <li>Object to or restrict certain processing, or withdraw consent where we rely on it; and</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            To exercise any of these rights, email us at
            <a href="mailto:@ContactEmail">@ContactEmail</a>. We will respond within 30 days and will not
            discriminate against you for exercising your rights. You can also revoke our access to your Google
            account at any time from your Google Account security settings, and you can opt out of Google
            Analytics using Google's
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out browser add-on</a>
            or by blocking cookies in your browser.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            We use a small number of cookies: essential cookies that keep you signed in and keep the Services
            secure, and analytics cookies set by Google Analytics. You can control cookies through your browser
            settings. Blocking essential cookies may prevent you from signing in.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>9. International Data Transfers</h2>
        <p>
            We are based in the United States, and our service providers may process data in the United States
            and other countries. If you use the Services from outside the United States, your information
            will be transferred to and processed in countries whose data protection laws may differ from yours.
            Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards, such as our providers' standard contractual
            clauses.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            The Services are not directed to children under 13 (or under 16 where that is the minimum age in
            your country), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child
            has given us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>11. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>
            The Services may link to websites or services we don't operate. We are not responsible for their
            privacy practices, so please review their policies.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the effective date
            above, and if the changes are significant we will give you notice, for example on the website or by email.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle your information, email
            <a href="mailto:@ContactEmail">@ContactEmail</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="legal-meta">
            See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    private const string EffectiveDate = "November 26, 2026";
    private const string ContactEmail = "contact@greensquirrel.dev";
}
